<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19862" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grandĭno</span></b> , āre,
		1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v.
				impers.</i> [id.], <i>to hail.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quare hieme ningat, non grandinet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 4, 4, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Aur. Vict. Vir. Ill. 73,
			7</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: sagittis, plumbo et saxis
			grandinat, nivit, Pac. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 507,
			28</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>To hail upon</i>: vinea grandinata est, August. ap.
			Psa. 49.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
